# shadcn + Tailwind v4

The active component and styling system is **shadcn/ui** (source in `components/ui/`) + **Tailwind CSS v4**. It replaces Astryx (ADR-018 superseded). This is one system, not coexistence with Astryx or StyleX.

## CLI

This project uses pnpm. Add or change primitives with:

- `pnpm exec shadcn <cmd>` — CLI already in `devDependencies`
- `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest <cmd>` — only when the latest CLI is needed

Examples: `pnpm exec shadcn add button`, `pnpm exec shadcn docs dialog`, `pnpm exec shadcn search sheet`.

Do not run `astryx ...`. Do not install the community Tailwind MCP. Configuration lives in `components.json` (Radix, RSC, lucide, CSS = `app/globals.css`).

## Setup

Already installed in `app/globals.css`: `tailwindcss`, `tw-animate-css`, and `shadcn/tailwind.css`. Tokens use `@theme inline`; `@custom-variant dark` maps to the `.dark` class, not OS preference. Default ship is dark (T-038.2). The light block is commented/held; do not delete the archive block. Keep `rz-theme` and `html.dark` (ADR-021). The chrome toggle stays hidden while on hold. Do not duplicate setup, and do not add `next-themes` as the default.

## Workflow

1. Check existing primitives in `components/ui/` and surfaces in `app/[locale]/_components/` before adding anything.
2. Use CLI `search` / `docs` before inventing a new overlay or form.
3. Page composition stays in `app/[locale]/_components/`. Generated files should be limited to `components/ui/` and `lib/utils.ts` (`cn`).
4. Do not add Sidebar, Chart, Command, Sonner, or Calendar just because the catalog has them. Brand chrome icons stay in `overlay-icons.tsx`.

## Styling

Preferred order:

1. Already-skinned shadcn primitives
2. Token-backed Tailwind utilities (`flex`, `flex-col`, `gap-8`, `bg-background`, `text-foreground`)
3. Scoped `className` + `app/globals.css` (`var(--spacing-*)`, `--chip-*`, `--color-accent`, `.home-*`, `.ct-*`, `.qi-*`, `.ps-*`, `.page-vt-*`)
4. `cn()` for conditional classes

- Use `gap-*`, `flex`, and `grid`; do not use `space-y-*`, `space-x-*`, or sibling margins for rhythm.
- Visual identity is **gothic-blood** (ADR-029): dark canvas, vellum, one blood accent; selected chrome uses outline (ADR-031). Not yellow pills, cream trays, or 3D elevation as identity.
- Overlay craft for Contact, Quick Info, and project sheet stays purposeful; do not fall back to default zinc/slate shadcn styling.
- No StyleX (`xstyle`, `stylex.create()`). The Turbopack compiler gap was closed by removing Astryx (T-037).
- No `style={{}}` for layout or color. The existing `colorScheme` on `<html>` is the exception.
- No random hex or arbitrary pixel values in JSX such as `bg-[#fff]` or `p-[13px]`.
- Use `!important` only when the same file already has a deliberate precedent, usually for theme-independent overlays.

## Overlays And Motion

Contact uses `Dialog`, Quick Info uses a right `Sheet`, and project details use a bottom `Drawer`; they are already skinned. Accessible titles are required. Identity motion uses `motion/react`; overlay enter/exit uses tokenized CSS transitions; Lenis stays. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

